   [campaign]    [soul] ORACLE decision: kind=action ctx={'place': 'You\'re in Fuchsia City — outdoors under open sky (a town with a Pokémon Center and a Mart).. From here: SOUTH → Route 19; EAST → Route 15 — wild Pokémon to catch/train; WEST → an unexplored area (unexplored). Places you\'ve been with wild Pokémon you can walk back to: Route 14; an unfamiliar area; Route 13. You can walk to anywhere you\'ve already been. Field moves ready: CUT.. Okay — to get past this I need HM Surf — the prize of the Safari Zone\'s Secret House, deep in the back area. Surf opens the sea: Cinnabar, the Seafoam route, and Victory Road\'s water. Heads up: you have ZERO Poké Balls — you literally can\'t catch a teammate until you buy some at a Mart, so a Mart run has to come before any catching.. You keep trying to regroup but the world hasn\'t changed in 3 turns - it went \'stuck\', and you don\'t seem to be getting anywhere.. HOW POKÉMON WORKS (what you\'re playing for): the GOAL is to earn 8 Gym Badges, beat the Elite Four, and roll the credits — that\'s beating the game. You build a TEAM of up to 6 Pokémon you like AND that cover each other (types/roles) — a solo carry with a dead-weight bench is a losing setup; a real trainer fields a balanced, levelled squad. CATCHING wild Pokémon is central (\'gotta catch \'em all\') — you catch to build that team and to fill the Pokédex. When you meet a wild Pokémon, weigh it: is it cool/strong/useful, does it cover a gap, is it better than a bench-warmer? — keep your best ~6, and build a squad you actually like. THE ARC: build a team -> beat the 8 gyms prepared -> Elite Four -> credits. ALSO NORMAL: you entered your own name (and your rival\'s) when the game began — people in this world knowing your names is ordinary, not a mystery to react to. RIGHT NOW your team is thin/lopsided (a strong lead but weak or too few others) — that\'s why tough trainers wall you. Building up a real squad (catch a good new teammate, level the weak ones) is how a prepared trainer gets past these. THE MAIN QUEST IS A FIXED PATH you\'re always on: beat the 8 Gym Leaders in order, then the Elite Four, then you win the game. You\'re on GYM 7 of 8 — next is Blaine in Cinnabar Island. The road forward leads there: until you\'ve won you are ALWAYS making progress toward the next gym. Grinding/catching/detours are fine — but ONLY with a clear purpose, and then you GET BACK ON THE ROAD to Cinnabar Island. Never just circle the same grass. ⚠️ ORDER OF OPERATIONS: before Blaine, HM Surf — the prize of the Safari Zone\'s Secret House, deep in the back area. Surf opens the sea: Cinnabar, the Seafoam route, and Victory Road\'s water — that errand comes FIRST (it unblocks the road and the trainers along it are exactly the training you need). Blaine is step two, not a competing choice. Word on the road about Blaine: the old fire scientist — FIRE-types on a volcano island; water washes him out YOUR STORY SO FAR (what you\'ve actually done — your past, not the future): Six badges: only Blaine on Cinnabar (Volcano) and Giovanni in Viridian (Earth) stand between you and the Elite Four road.. Next on my list: catch an growlithe around Route 7 / Route 8. It grows into my arcanine — that\'s my answer for Champion down the line. Grabbing it now, before I need it.. THINGS YOU\'VE HEARD AND READ (from people and signs — your own notes, use them when they point somewhere): "I had a vision of your arrival. I have had psychic powers since I was a child. It started when a spoon I carelessly tossed, bent. I dislike battling, but if you"; "Sealed within that TM06 lies TOXIC! It is a secret technique dating back some four hundred years."; "KIRA put the TM06 in the TM CASE."; "KIRA received TM06 from KOGA.". YOUR PLAN — right now: You\'re ready — stop grinding and head to Cinnabar Island for the Volcano Badge. Next: You CRUSHED Sabrina — ride the momentum: Blaine in Cinnabar Island is NEXT (not fought yet); the trainers on the way are your training. Bigger picture: Reach Cinnabar Island, beat Blaine for the Volcano Badge. Your team right now: blastoise (L57), rattata (L18), abra the kadabra (L19), diglett (L18), lapras (L25). Remember YOU are the one playing this — narrate your plan to chat in your own voice (first person: "I\'m grinding", "my team"), and never ask anyone what you\'re doing or who\'s on your team — you know.', 'progress': "6 badge(s) earned (Boulder, Cascade, Thunder, Rainbow, Soul, Marsh). Next gym: Blaine of Cinnabar Island. Pokédex: 13 caught. She's six badges down, only two to go (of 8 badges, then the Elite Four).", 'party': 'blastoise (L57), rattata (L18), abra the kadabra (L19), diglett (L18), lapras (L25)', 'goal': {'short': "You're ready — stop grinding and head to Cinnabar Island for the Volcano Badge", 'medium': 'You CRUSHED Sabrina — ride the momentum: Blaine in Cinnabar Island is NEXT (not fought yet); the trainers on the way are your training', 'long': 'Reach Cinnabar Island, beat Blaine for the Volcano Badge'}, 'strategy': "1) WAR PREP: next is Blaine (fire, ~L42-47). Your answer on the team: blastoise — lead with it and keep it healthy.\n2) TEAM BUILD: growlithe -> arcanine answers Champion.\n3) DEX PUSH: 13/50 species caught — at 50 the Route 15 aide (by Fuchsia) hands over the EXP. SHARE (the whole bench levels off every fight). Catch every NEW species you cross; never wander just to hunt.\n4) ICE BEAM FUND: ¥58,322 short of the Game Corner TM13 budget (~¥80,500 total). Ice Beam on the ace freezes everything left — Venusaur, Lance's dragons, the birds. Fight your battles for the payouts, sell loot at marts, buy supplies but never splurge. It arms itself when funded.\n5) STANDING ORDERS: the goal is ROLL CREDITS. Forward progress beats wandering; heal beats fighting hurt; type advantage decides fights; build the planned team, not just the ace."} options=['regroup']

